From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:34:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 346/371] family server: a quest choice finished over several
 visits closes, so a pirate who logged out halfway gets the next quests

A quest choice (Tia Dalma's four doll materials, wdr2Materials: Straw / Pitch / Silk / Wire) keeps each finished
quest until the others are done. At log-in QuestStub.linkQuest left a finished quest complete=False and not
processed, so QuestChoice.isComplete counted only the hand-ins of the current visit and the choice never closed
for a pirate who logged out halfway (claude2 100000004: 23101-23104 in the ladder history, the choice 19901 not,
no blood quests).

QuestStub.linkQuest now marks a finished quest of a choice as done again when the ladder history already has it
(it was handed in on an earlier visit), and QuestManagerAI.finishHeldChoice, run from activateQuests' callback,
closes a choice that is complete at log-in through the normal handleQuestComplete (history updated, the next
quests swapped in, tracked when they arrive). One per log-in. The client copy of QuestLadder.py is not changed;
only the AI links the quests. Offline sim with the real QuestLadder / QuestStatus.updateHistory on the WeaponDoll
ladder (places' sim_choice_relogin.py): HEAD FAIL (4: two-visit choice never closes, 19901 never in history,
stuck save gets no swap, Straw paid twice), patched PASS (all 5 cases, one-visit and finished-but-never-handed-in
unchanged). AI only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/quest/QuestLadder.py    | 15 +++++++++++++++
 pirates/quest/QuestManagerAI.py | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 48 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pirates/quest/QuestLadder.py b/pirates/quest/QuestLadder.py
index e7bfee6..5ab66e3 100644
--- a/pirates/quest/QuestLadder.py
+++ b/pirates/quest/QuestLadder.py
@@ -407,6 +407,21 @@ class QuestStub(QuestContainer):
                 self.acceptOnce(quest.getDroppedEventString(), self.handleQuestDropped)
 
             self.complete = False
+            # family server (0430): a quest choice keeps each finished quest until the others are done too (Tia
+            # Dalma's four doll materials). After a log-out the finished ones came back as never handed in, so the
+            # choice counted only those finished in this visit and never closed: a pirate who logged out halfway
+            # could never get past the materials. A finished quest the ladder history already has was handed back
+            # in an earlier visit: it is done again, as it was.
+            parent = self.parent
+            if parent is not None and parent.isChoice() and quest.isComplete():
+                history = self.av.getQuestLadderHistory() if self.av else []
+                if self.getQuestInt() in history:
+                    self.complete = True
+                    self.processed = True
+                    self.completedQuests = [quest]
+                    if quest not in parent.completedQuests:
+                        parent.updateCompletedQuests(quest)
+
             return True
         else:
             return False
diff --git a/pirates/quest/QuestManagerAI.py b/pirates/quest/QuestManagerAI.py
index 0f848ca..5a69bac 100644
--- a/pirates/quest/QuestManagerAI.py
+++ b/pirates/quest/QuestManagerAI.py
@@ -322,12 +322,44 @@ class QuestManagerAI(DirectObject):
 
     def activateQuests(self, avatar, callback=None):
         def _questsActivatedCallback(*args, **kwargs):
-            self.trackQuestIfNone(avatar)
+            # the swap a closed choice starts tracks its new quests when they arrive
+            if not self.finishHeldChoice(avatar):
+                self.trackQuestIfNone(avatar)
             if callback:
                 callback(*args, **kwargs)
 
         self.runQuestFSM(ActivateQuestsFSM, avatar, callback=_questsActivatedCallback)
 
+    def finishHeldChoice(self, avatar):
+        # family server (0430): a quest choice whose quests were all handed back over several visits never closed
+        # (each visit counted only its own), so the pirate kept the finished quests and never got the next ones
+        # (claude2 held all four of Tia Dalma's doll materials). The ladder copies now remember them at log-in
+        # (QuestStub.linkQuest); close such a choice once its quests are here, as its last hand-in would have.
+        # One per log-in: the next quests come from a quest FSM, and only one runs at a time.
+        questStatus = getattr(avatar, 'questStatus', None)
+        if questStatus is None:
+            return False
+
+        history = avatar.getQuestLadderHistory()
+        for ladder in list(questStatus.ladders.values()):
+            choices = []
+            ladder.getChoiceContainers(choices)
+            for choice in choices:
+                held = choice.completedQuests
+                if choice.getQuestInt() in history or not held or choice.getParent() is None:
+                    continue
+
+                if not choice.isComplete() or not all(self.getQuest(avatar, questDoId=quest.doId) is quest
+                                                      for quest in held):
+                    continue
+
+                self.notify.info('avatar %d: closing quest choice %s held over a log-out (%s)'
+                                 % (avatar.doId, choice.getName(), [quest.getQuestId() for quest in held]))
+                choice.getParent().handleQuestComplete(held[-1], choice, held)
+                return True
+
+        return False
+
     def trackQuestIfNone(self, avatar):
         # the arrow and the beam follow only the tracked (active) quest. Handing a quest in drops it, which
         # clears the tracked quest, and the next quests the ladder swaps in were never tracked: from the third
